  "chapter_note": "This chapter is dominated by Manichaean ecclesial application — almost the entire second half concerns the catechumen, his fasting, prayer, alms, faith, and the choosing of forms by the Apostle/Elect. The substratic core appears in the opening question/answer about the ten ways drawing from the Zone (four ascending to the Light, eight others, with the Error transmuted into three ways pouring into Gehenna), and the three-fold enumeration of the Gehenna-paths: lawlessness, killing, and the wounding word that mocks the gods. After segment 23 the chapter pivots entirely to the catechumen's salvation, illustrated by two extended pastoral similes (horse with king's seal; man journeying to a city with his comitatus). Heavy editorial overlay throughout the latter portion.",
